assName\":\"space-y-4 text-ink/65 font-body leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"I was born into very humble beginnings with my gift and insights. At age 8 or 9, my grandmother who raised me bought a set of paints and brushes — she was tired of me painting every possible space under our elevated home on concrete blocks. From the onset of this simple and not so obvious present, my journey as an artist began without the aid of any formal training.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"I always determined to myself to be an artist of note. My grandmother and childhood friends saw in me something special, even when I doubted my path.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"With all of the distractions of growing into adulthood, I never relinquished my desire to create scenes from my immediate green lushness and very colorful surroundings. I was and still am an avid devotee of sunsets and unusual land formations.\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-gold/20 via-gold/10 to-transparent\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gold tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-body mb-4\",\"children\":\"The Journey\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display text-4xl text-ink mb-6\",\"children\":[\"From the Atlantic Coast\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-celestial italic\",\"children\":\"to Santa Barbara\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4 text-ink/65 font-body leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"My early career was identified with landscapes and seascapes. I was born on the Atlantic coast of South America in a small country called Guyana — land of waters. By my late 20s I migrated to the United States to pursue an undergraduate degree in Communication and the Arts, which I completed successfully.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"I then moved to graduate school at the University of California at Santa Barbara, where I completed my Master of Fine Arts. It was during this foray that my artwork took what some called a dramatic detour into the world of magical realism — a juxtaposition of what we commonly call the real world alongside the world of an otherworldly consciousness.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"I identified with the freedom to express myself in ways that were not governed by the conventions of classical and contemporary western art parlance and expression.\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-gold/20 via-gold/10 to-transparent\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gold tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-body mb-4\",\"children\":\"The Philosophy\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display text-4xl text-ink mb-6\",\"children\":[\"Symbolic Logic &\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-ember italic\",\"children\":\"Dream Consciousness\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4 text-ink/65 font-body leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The creation of symbolic logic took center stage as I reflected on objects I was familiar with but turned them into symbols of how I viewed the world — in a word, my consciousness. Sky and water were no longer separate entities; they became fluid and interchangeable for me. Land formations and atmospheric conditions were assigned to different locations in the world I created from my imagination.\"}],\"$L17\",\"$L18\"]}]]}],\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"relative border-t border-whisper bg-vellum\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-96 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-gold/30 to-transparent\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-16\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-12 mb-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display text-3xl text-ink mb-2\",\"children\":\"Clinton Crawford\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-dusk/50 tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4\",\"children\":\"Professor Emeritus · MFA · Artist\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-dusk/70 font-body leading-relaxed max-w-xs\",\"children\":\"Born in Guyana, South America. Works in magical realism exploring portals between real and imagined worlds.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display text-xl text-gold mb-4 tracking-wide\",\"children\":\"Explore\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/gallery\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6\",null,{\"href\":\"/gallery\",\"className\":\"text-dusk/60 hover:text-ink text-sm font-body transition-colors duration-200 tracking-wide\",\"children\":\"Gallery\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/gallery?series=Portals+to+Other+Dimensions\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6\",null,{\"href\":\"/gallery?series=Portals+to+Other+Dimensions\",\"className\":\"text-dusk/60 hover:text-ink text-sm font-body transition-colors duration-200 tracking-wide\",\"children\":\"Portals Series\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/about\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6\",null,{\"href\":\"/about\",\"className\":\"text-dusk/60 hover:text-ink text-sm font-body transition-colors duration-200 tracking-wide\",\"children\":\"About the Artist\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/cart\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6\",null,{\"href\":\"/cart\",\"className\":\"text-dusk/60 hover:text-ink text-sm font-body transition-colors duration-200 tracking-wide\",\"children\":\"Cart\"}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display text-xl text-gold mb-4 tracking-wide\",\"children\":\"Acquire a Work\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-dusk/60 font-body mb-4 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Interested in a piece or a commission? All inquiries are handled with care.\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:inquiries@clintoncrawfordart.com\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-blush hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-200\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"inquiries@clintoncrawfordart.com\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"→\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-dusk/40 mt-4 font-body\",\"children\":\"Based in the United States. Ships worldwide.\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-gold/20 to-transparent mb-8\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-dusk/40 font-body tracking-wide\",\"children\":[\"© \",2026,\" Dr. Clinton Crawford. All rights reserved.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-dusk/35 font-body italic\",\"children\":\"\\\"I have learnt to let go and not insist on controlling the outcome.\\\"\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"$L1c\",null,{\"children\":[\"$L1d\",[\"$\",\"$L1e\",null,{\"promise\":\"$@1f\"}]]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The vivid, vibrant colors in my work are influenced by being born near the equator, where light plays a dominant role in one's sensibilities. My palette is reflective of that experience, even though I am more than four decades removed from that tropical sphere.\"}]\n18:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Generally I let my canvas and initial brush strokes guide my composition. The images evince from the uncensored interplay with my dream consciousness state and my lived experiences. Light and dark contrasts are used to create a dramatic platform upon which the viewer can be a participant.\"}]\n19:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-gold/20 via-gold/10 to-transparent\"}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"glass-card p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-gold tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-body mb-4\",\"children\":\"Artist Statement\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4 text-dusk/70 font-body leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"These works belong to a series of twelve that illustrate \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"Portals to Other Dimensions\"}],\". I am aligned with a literary and artistic philosophical tradition called Magical Realism: a juxtaposition of real and imagined worlds.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Born in Guyana, South America, I have been a painter from the early age of seven. My voluminous collection is largely done with oils on canvas. However, the works in the \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"Portals\"}],\" series are acrylics on canvas.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"As a specialist in classical African Civilizations, my works are also informed by my travels to the Nile Valley and beyond. Symbolic logic is at the base of my creation — life begins with an egg of some sort, hence it reoccurs in my expression. Without water, there is no life.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display text-xl text-ink/80 italic border-l-2 border-gold/30 pl-4 ml-0\",\"children\":\"\\\"Now in my mid-seventies, I continue to learn and heed the voice from within. I have learnt to let go and not insist on controlling the outcome. It's the most liberating feeling one can experience.\\\"\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-whisper\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-display text-xl text-gold\",\"children\":\"Dr. Clinton Crawford\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-dusk/50 font-body tracking-widest uppercase mt-1\",\"children\":\"Professor Emeritus · Painter · Scholar\"}]]}]]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 pt-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L6\",null,{\"href\":\"/gallery\",\"className\":\"btn-portal\",\"children\":\"Browse the Gallery\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:inquiries@clintoncrawfordart.com\",\"className\":\"btn-ghost\",\"children\":\"Commission a Work\"}]]}]\n13:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]\n1d:null\n1f:{\"metadata\":[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"About the Artist | Clinton Crawford Art\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Dr. Clinton Crawford — Professor Emeritus, MFA, painter of magical realism. Born in Guyana. Self-taught from age 7. Works explore portals between real and imagined worlds.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"2\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"Clinton Crawford,magical realism,fine art,paintings,Guyana artist,Portals to Other Dimensions\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Dr. Clinton Crawford | Portals to Other Dimensions\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Original paintings exploring the threshold between real and imagined worlds.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"property\":\"og:site_name\",\"content\":\"Clinton Crawford Art\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"website\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"Dr. Clinton Crawford | Portals to Other Dimensions\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Original paintings exploring the threshold between real and imagined worlds.\"}]],\"error\":null,\"digest\":\"$undefined\"}\n16:\"$1f:metadata\"\n"}